abstract: >-
  DEGexplorer is an R/Shiny application for running and exploring RNA-seq
  differential analyses. It runs DESeq2, limma-voom, edgeR and EBSeq on gene
  or transcript counts, tests differential transcript usage with edgeR / limma
  diffSplice, DEXSeq, DRIMSeq and satuRn, and offers stage-wise testing with
  stageR, each configured as recommended by the method's authors. Results are
  explored through volcano, MA, scatter, PCA and heatmap figures, GO / KEGG /
  MSigDB enrichment with a gallery of publication figures, and a gene
  intelligence panel. Every analysis can be exported with a run record and an R
  script that reproduces it.
keywords:
  - RNA-seq
  - differential expression
  - differential transcript usage
  - Shiny
  - Bioconductor
  - DESeq2
  - edgeR
  - limma
  - enrichment analysis
  - reproducible research
